      "rationale": "U+2028 LINE SEPARATOR is not in the covered-whitespace class (_WS = [\\t\\n\\r ]) that every salary grammar boundary uses, unlike bare backslash-s which Python's re treats as matching it. This is a newly authored record for Slice 2: the existing 261ffe3 correction round fixed findings 2-5, all of which build on this covered-whitespace narrowing, but none of its own fixtures isolates this specific guard on its own (each is independently rejected by its own boundary check regardless of this guard's state). Traced directly against salary.py's _WS constant and _LABEL_PREFIX."
